This project was a dive into Godot. Objective was simple : familiarize with this game engine through a minimal 2D survivor game creation. 

Godot mechanics used here:
- Physic through character, mobs and projectiles collisions
- TileMapLayer and pathfinding base on navigation polygon baking at runtime (with information from TileMapLayer)
- Singleton aka global class usable from any scene
- Animating a cut-out with AnimationPlayer and Skeleton2D
- A little bit of UI (very very very minimal)

Game systems:
- Procedural world generation with tiles
- Skill or stats up on level up
- Elemental state diffusion through mob, projectiles, enemies and tiles (system of "LogicTile" needed)
- Mobs spawn outside of the viewport but not too far
- Dodge mechanic
- Two spells : fire who make DoT and burn trees (they disapear after a while) and water which heal the player
- Mobs quantity who evolve according to a ease in function
